  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/adm600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Adm 606.10 Awards Not To Be Made by Line Item",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Adm 606.10 Awards Not To Be Made by Line Item. If an RFP, RFQ, RFB, or other form of purchasing request contains reference to more than one item, vendors shall be selected or recommended on the basis of the selection criteria as applied to the RFP, RFB, RFQ, or other purchasing request as a whole, rather than by applying those criteria to each individual item or line item sought by the state.\n\nSource. #8310, eff 5-11-05; ss by #10364, eff 7-1-13; ss by #13708, eff 7-29-23 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Adm 600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/adm600.html"
